<!--
  Generated by tools/zh_from_xcstrings.py from values/strings_notifications.xml,
  then hand-filled. Two groups come back MISSING from that script and are the
  ones to check after a regeneration:

  - everything carrying a format specifier, because upstream's catalog keys use
    `%@`/`%lld` and Android needs `%1$s`/`%1$d`. Their Chinese below is
    upstream's, with the placeholders re-indexed — not re-translated.
  - everything with an escaped apostrophe, because Android XML writes `\'` and
    the script looks up the literal English including the backslash.

  The channel names, the channel descriptions and the Health Connect rationale
  have no upstream counterpart at all — iOS has no notification channels and no
  Health Connect — so those were written for this port.

  See the English file's header for why a notification already in the alarm
  queue keeps the language it was scheduled in.
-->
